WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.362
If your income stopped tomorrow, how would your family carry on?

2
00:00:05.462 --> 00:00:08.456
Life insurance pays a sum to the beneficiaries you choose,

3
00:00:08.643 --> 00:00:13.600
so they do not have to sell the home, stop studying or take on debt.

4
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.220
How much cover do you need?

5
00:00:16.685 --> 00:00:19.054
Add up your loans, the income your family would

6
00:00:19.054 --> 00:00:22.234
need for as long as it matters, and goals such as studies,

7
00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:24.649
then take away what you already have.

8
00:00:25.749 --> 00:00:29.010
Term insurance is the most economical way to a large sum.

9
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.727
Whole-of-life cover lasts your whole life.

10
00:00:31.914 --> 00:00:35.744
And life insurance with savings combines cover with capital.

11
00:00:36.844 --> 00:00:40.558
In Cyprus, life premiums are deductible from taxable income,

12
00:00:40.861 --> 00:00:46.003
up to seven per cent of the sum insured, within the overall cap of one fifth.

13
00:00:47.103 --> 00:00:50.051
A common mistake is having only the cover the bank asked for.

14
00:00:50.296 --> 00:00:51.734
It pays off the loan;

15
00:00:51.828 --> 00:00:54.451
it leaves no income for your family.

16
00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:58.082
Work out an estimate of your cover with the free tool

17
00:00:58.082 --> 00:01:01.878
on avrastro.com, and go through it with an advisor.
